    "chapters": [
      {
        "title": "Overview",
        "tiles": [
          {
            "kind": "note",
            "title": "Design system",
            "text": "Design system\n\n## Principles\n- Clear before clever: every screen says what it is for in its first line.\n- One way to do one thing: a colour, a size or a component has one name.\n- Calm by default: colour is for meaning, never for decoration.\n\n## Using tokens\nUse a token by its name, never its value. Change the value here and every screen follows. Each colour shows its light and dark values and is checked against the colour it is read on.\n\n## Using components\nBuild screens from the components in this system. When one is missing, add it to Components with a short note on where it is needed.\n\n## Accessibility\nText reaches 4.5:1 against what it sits on; large text and icons 3:1. Focus is always visible. Nothing is told by colour alone.\n",
            "size": {
              "w": 1020,
              "h": 620
            }
          }
        ]
      },
